{
	"id": "pattern_loom",
	"name": "Pattern Loom",
	"description": "A sci-fi loom that manufactures wallpaper. The 17 wallpaper groups become output — a carpet woven on glowing warp threads and fed continuously out of the machine, the symmetry group scrolling past like fabric off a mill. Re-bodies the pattern editors (pattern_maker_station, pattern_tile_plate, vr_tile_editor) as a machine: those edit the carpet, this manufactures it. Reuses PatternSim.render_to_image and machine vocabulary from props-dna-gallery.",
	"category": "dna_grammar",
	"theoreticalGrounding": "A pattern is produced, not given. The wallpaper group is the program; the loom is the press that runs it. loom_style (roller | warp | mirror) gives the same wallpaper engine three machine bodies.",
